        "original_id": "f1caf543-9ecf-5d90-b9d9-b2a497dbd299",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gustave-Hippolyte Roger, Hector Berlioz, Giacomo Meyerbeer, Daniel Auber\n- Works: La damnation de Faust, Le prophète, L'enfant prodigue\n- Places: Opéra-Comique, Paris\n- Roles: leading tenor roles, Azaël\n\nFacts:\n- Gustave-Hippolyte Roger created the leading tenor role in Hector Berlioz's La damnation de Faust in 1846.\n- La damnation de Faust was first performed at the Opéra-Comique in Paris on 6 December 1846.\n- Gustave-Hippolyte Roger created the leading tenor role in Giacomo Meyerbeer's Le prophète in 1849.\n- Gustave-Hippolyte Roger, a French tenor who lived from 1815 to 1879, sang the role of Azaël in the premiere of Daniel Auber's L'enfant prodigue.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
